cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AUDRE
abstract: >-
  AUDRE (Analyzing Usage, Depth, Resource intensity, and Engagement) is a
  reproducible, privacy-aware pipeline for turning enterprise generative-AI chat
  telemetry into context-specific usage representations and candidate workflow
  hypotheses.
type: software
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/GSA/audre-workflows
keywords:
  - generative artificial intelligence
  - enterprise telemetry
  - workflow analysis
  - network analysis
  - privacy
  - public sector

authors:
  - given-names: Perla
    family-names: Molina
    email: perlam@stanford.edu
    affiliation: Stanford University
  - given-names: Isabel
    family-names: Metzger
    email: isabel.metzger@gsa.gov
    affiliation: U.S. General Services Administration
  - given-names: Zachary
    family-names: Whitman
    email: zach.whitman@gsa.gov
    affiliation: U.S. General Services Administration
  - given-names: Richard
    family-names: Speidel
    email: richard.speidel@gsa.gov
    affiliation: U.S. General Services Administration

# Cite the paper rather than the software. The CFF specification only permits
# `software` or `dataset` as the top-level type, so a paper cannot be the root
# object; `preferred-citation` is the mechanism that redirects citation tools
# (including GitHub's "Cite this repository") to the publication.
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper (see
  preferred-citation below).

